# The refusal each conformance corpus file has, as our parser
# produces it. `-` is a file that parses clean; anything else is
# the distinct refusal codes it produced, in tree order.
#
# KEYED ON FILE NAME, not path, and the numeric prefixes are
# stripped. A file moving between tiers or renumbering within one
# is the `t/` sweep working, and must not read as a regression.
# The per-tier adjacency fixture carries its tier, since fourteen
# tiers each hold one and they are different files.
#
# 113 files, 99 clean, 14 refusing.
#
# Regenerate with -conformance.update-ratchet and commit the result
# WITH the change that moved it. A baseline updated on its own is a
# number nobody can attribute.
